1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,100
I'm so over this. It's way too hot. Kojo, aren't you dying to go and cool off somewhere?

2
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,820
I wouldn't mind.

3
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:16,700
Hello and welcome.

4
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:21,060
Oh wow, I've never been to a manga cafe before.

5
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:29,060
Aw, you poor thing. Well, I highly recommend them. It's always nice and cool inside, there's food and drinks, and of course, you can read anything you want.

6
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:31,280
But, it's pretty much paradise.

7
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:37,500
Oh, sounds great. Except... we're so close!

8
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:40,400
I love how much room there is to stretch your legs!

9
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:42,520
I... I, uh...

10
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:07,920
I lost it.

11
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:37,900
Thank you.

12
00:01:37,920 --> 00:02:07,900
Thank you.

13
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:09,920
Thank you.

14
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:38,920
I was just wondering.

15
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,740
Check it out. You hungry?

16
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:45,340
Huh? Everything on this menu is gigantic!

17
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,980
I almost forgot I brought this one with me.

18
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:51,140
I'm giving it a hardcore wreck. You have to read it.

19
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:57,360
I'm a mega best-selling high school student, light novel author that has a succubus thirsting for me every night and I don't know what to do.

20
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,980
Were all of those words part of the title?

21
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,880
Or Suck-Eye Decay. Four-panel slice of life.

22
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,500
What's a slice of life?

23
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:09,800
Hmm, it's like when nothing really happens, but that's what's so great about it. Just a nice, tranquil story with cherries on top.

24
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:13,400
So the characters just do normal things and people like to read about that?

25
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:19,140
Yeah, exactly right. Slice of life stuff is all warm and fuzzy, so it makes for great bedtime reading.

26
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:25,780
In Suck-Eye Decay, the main guy Kaname stays up all night writing light novels, so like he never gets any rest.

27
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,500
Then Liz, who's a succubus, makes it her mission to try to get him to sleep.

28
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:31,860
Look how cute her mini pigtails are!

29
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:36,180
That's like a ginormous weakness of mine. I always fall for characters who have them.

30
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:37,520
You mean her hairstyle?

31
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:46,760
That's why I have such a crush on Juju! I seriously want to cosplay Liz something fierce! I love her so hard! I mean, look at her! She is a dwarves!

32
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:54,080
Veronica does show a lot of skin. I promise to be more sensitive when I pick the next character.

33
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,080
At least there's more to this cosplay than Veronica's.

34
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,060
Not saying I'd actually do it, but you know.

35
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,560
Why wouldn't you? The amount of skin she shows?

36
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,520
Seriously? Dude, have we met?

37
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:05,840
She's got a point.

38
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:09,640
I mean, I love the heck out of Liz, but her mini pigtails are a problem.

39
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:12,980
They're what make her so adorable, but I couldn't pull them off.

40
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:16,280
Only little pixie-like girlies can rock that.

41
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:19,080
I'd go up in flames if I tried. Know what I mean?

42
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:24,700
Uh, what? Why the psycho stare? Is there something on my face?

43
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:29,380
I just... I was picturing it, and I think you'd look nice.

44
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:31,820
You honestly don't agree?

45
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:38,660
I mean, I know you didn't think you could cosplay Xiontan since she's a little kid,

46
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,880
but this is just a hairstyle, right?

47
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:41,900
Mm-hmm.

48
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:45,520
So why not go for it, then? Couldn't hurt to try.

49
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,840
Besides, you really seem to love her.

50
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:59,580
Um, I mean, I trust your judgment on these kinds of things.

51
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,560
S-so maybe for you.

52
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,180
You should.

53
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:05,720
Mm-hmm.

54
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:10,560
She really did look amazing as both Shizuku-tan and Black Lobelia,

55
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,740
so I know she doesn't have anything to worry about.

56
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:16,380
By the way, you said Liz was something called a succubus?

57
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,600
I've never heard that term.

58
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:21,080
Well, the short explanation is that they're lady demons.

59
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:21,540
Cool.

60
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:24,040
They make dudes have sexy time dreams,

61
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,560
and then they suck out all of their man juice and kill them.

62
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:29,360
In what world is that tranquil bedtime reading?

63
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:31,520
Yes, Gojo?

64
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:36,220
Would you say this one's more of a slice of seriously disturbed life?

65
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,060
Let me think.

66
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:37,540
No.

67
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:38,480
Next question.

68
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:39,980
Just read it.

69
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:40,660
It's peaceful.

70
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,060
How could a demon that kills you in your sleep be peaceful?

71
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:45,800
This is a relaxing escape.

72
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,200
Lullaby.

73
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:49,080
Hey!

74
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,700
Go to sleep already!

75
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:52,360
Yeah, yeah, yeah, mister!

76
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:53,440
I know.

77
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,680
I'll sing a lullaby so he'll get sleepy.

78
00:05:55,680 --> 00:06:00,240
Rock-a-bye, baby, on the treetop.

79
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:04,400
I know who was a hale.

80
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:07,400
Chocolate.

81
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:09,500
You may be getting enough sleep at school,

82
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:11,960
but a backward sleep schedule is extremely bad for you.

83
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:13,800
Your autonomic nerves are gonna get all out of whack.

84
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,260
Now she decides to make sense.

85
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:18,440
Hey, succubus, I'll give you my midnight snack if you shut up.

86
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,200
Oh, really?

87
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,640
Thank you so much.

88
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,380
Yeah, you have milk filling, and they're super yummy.

89
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:27,840
I'm gonna go shanty's with the others.

90
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,260
You're right.

91
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:37,540
It does leave you with a warm, fuzzy feeling.

92
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,460
And she's so cute, doesn't it?

93
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:40,320
It's the best.

94
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:41,400
I knew you'd get it.

95
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:43,900
I'll be right back.

96
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,240
I'm gonna go grab some more books.

97
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:46,060
All right.

98
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,580
Slice of life.

99
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:50,880
I do get it.

100
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:52,340
It's nice.

101
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:52,380
It's nice.

102
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:55,620
Wait a minute.

103
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:58,140
This could be a problem.

104
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,580
The art style is cute and simplified.

105
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:03,200
How am I supposed to know how the clothes should drape?

106
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:05,660
There were parts I couldn't see on the other costumes,

107
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,440
but not to this extent.

108
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:10,180
I have no idea what the back looks like,

109
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,180
because it's always covered.

110
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:12,920
I see.

111
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,520
Depending on the series,

112
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:17,960
I may or may not be able to see the full details of the outfit.

113
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:26,780
I'll have to fill in the blanks and imagine them.

114
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:30,460
No way!

115
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:32,700
I didn't know it was sunset already.

116
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:34,180
Time flies.

117
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:35,700
We had such a lazy day today.

118
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:36,540
Yeah, I know.

119
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:37,740
But I had a lot of fun, though.

120
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:38,700
Yeah, me too.

121
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:40,780
Uh, Kitagawa?

122
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:41,920
Could we...

123
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:42,060
Huh?

124
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:44,520
Could we stop into a bookstore?

125
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,540
I really want to read Sakai DK.

126
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:48,240
Totally awesome, right?

127
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,640
I knew you'd get hooked.

128
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:51,200
I think there's one nearby.

129
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:51,840
Let's go.

130
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,640
There's also a clothing store.

131
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:02,340
You got some new Jinbei.

132
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:04,420
Perfect for this hot weather.

133
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:05,940
Good choice.

134
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:10,080
I actually got two sets.

135
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,340
This one looks great on you.

136
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:18,800
Grandpa, I...

137
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,980
I can't believe this.

138
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:22,700
It doesn't feel real.

139
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:27,100
I am currently at a love hotel.

140
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:28,900
The previous day.

141
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,520
I bought a swimsuit that looks like Liz's outfit,

142
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:32,760
and it's super cute.

143
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,340
I'm finished on my end as well.

144
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,140
For real?

145
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:37,300
Then you want to do Liz's photo shoot at a studio?

146
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,060
Your place is all Japanese style,

147
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,940
and the posters in my room are a bit yikes.

148
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:41,780
Hold up.

149
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:44,060
I found a studio that looks like Kaname's place,

150
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:45,620
and it's super close to you, Gojo.

151
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:46,380
Oh, damn!

152
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:48,080
It's only 5,900 yen.

153
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,000
It's so cheap.

154
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:51,580
I had no idea there was a photo studio near my house.

155
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:53,040
I reserved it so fast.

156
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,560
Can you meet me at the station tomorrow?

157
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:55,300
All right.

158
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:02,480
Are you sure there's really a studio in here?

159
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:03,960
Yeah, why not?

160
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:06,600
You got to pay first, so I'll go make that happen.

161
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,280
We're in room 303.

162
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:09,020
Wait.

163
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:11,760
They have more than 300 studios?

164
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,120
Here we are.

165
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,760
Oh, damn!

166
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:26,620
This bed is huge!

167
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:27,600
Like, everywhere size!

168
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,700
I mean, if you're a famous light novel author,

169
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,140
your bed better be this big!

170
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,540
There's so much room, but it's, like, simple, you know?

171
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,740
It looks just like Kaname's room!

172
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:37,100
Whoa!

173
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:38,340
OMG!

174
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,760
Is that what I think it is?

175
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:40,760
Yeah, dude.

176
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:42,480
Pretty sure we got a room in a love hotel.

177
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:43,420
Oh, well.

178
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,220
Whatever works.

179
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:46,720
What's the matter with you, bro?

180
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:48,200
Oh, uh, nothing at all.

181
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:50,400
It's just that far a second there.

182
00:09:51,020 --> 00:09:52,580
I thought you said we're in a love hotel.

183
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:53,220
Yep.

184
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,020
Isn't it cool?

185
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,780
You didn't tell me that!

186
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:58,500
These are the things I'd like to be aware of!

187
00:09:58,660 --> 00:09:59,620
Why are we in a love hotel?

188
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,220
Do you know what goes on in these places?

189
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:02,880
Not photography or in these...

190
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:03,880
I guess I got too excited.

191
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,400
I saw Kaname's bed online and just clicked.

192
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:08,680
It said we could take cosplay photos.

193
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:09,800
And it's stupid cheap!

194
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:11,460
So I insta-reserved, because hello!

195
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,220
And that brings us to now!

196
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:16,540
I didn't realize what it was until we were outside looking at the place.

197
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:17,660
And now we're locked in!

198
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,400
Sad emoji!

199
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:21,220
I guess it pays to read the fine print, huh?

200
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,440
Of course!

201
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,080
This is classic Kitaka!

202
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:28,440
But besides that, oopsie, I'd say we lucked out!

203
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:29,640
I mean, look around!

204
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:31,420
Is this not Toad's Kaname style?

205
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:36,280
I can make this work.

206
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:38,880
All I have to do is imagine it's a studio.

207
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:41,820
If only that were possible!

208
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:44,680
I'm not creative enough to ignore all of this!

209
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,560
The abandoned hospital I could deal with!

210
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:48,760
But I can't just pretend this stuff isn't here!

211
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:52,000
This room is crawling with adult paraphernalia!

212
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,140
I can't take it anymore!

213
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,440
I'm getting dizzy!

214
00:10:57,180 --> 00:11:01,060
Just thinking about being in a love hotel with Kitagawa is more than I can handle!

215
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:06,760
To be honest, I've been curious about what these places are like.

216
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:09,100
I know some cosplayers who have sleepovers here.

217
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:10,620
And it sounds like a blast!

218
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,300
Girls' night at a love hotel?

219
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,160
Yeah!

220
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:14,600
See, doesn't that look rad?

221
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:17,420
You can even get a discount if you bring a large group!

222
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:18,740
I guess you're right.

223
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:20,600
They do look like they're having fun.

224
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:21,620
For sure!

225
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:23,740
Is that a bunch of bread underneath?

226
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:24,300
Yep!

227
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,800
I think they have it here, too!

228
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:27,780
Do you have a sweet tooth, Gojo?

229
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:29,680
Well, sometimes I eat candy.

230
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,380
But it's usually just when I'm working.

231
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:34,260
Chocolate's good when you're working on stuff that takes brain power.

232
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,920
That's why Kaname eats it so much.

233
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:36,520
Ah!

234
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:38,920
I was wondering why he was always eating those things.

235
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:40,320
Let's order some food!

236
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,560
Okay, thanks!

237
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:44,040
That actually sounds like a horrible idea!

238
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,200
That performance was a 10 out of 10.

239
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:48,240
Look, I know it was an honest mistake,

240
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:51,120
but we're both minors, so we're not even supposed to be in here!

241
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:53,140
Well, that might be true if we were normies.

242
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,660
What? We are normies!

243
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,220
Okay, fine, you win.

244
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:57,860
Sometimes my ideas suck.

245
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:00,980
Now that that's done, I'll go change!

246
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:02,120
What? Why?

247
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:04,580
Because the whole point was to cosplay!

248
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:07,600
It would be a huge waste of money if we didn't do it now, right?

249
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:08,960
Oh, you're serious.

250
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,780
Oh my god, look at this bathtub!

251
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,720
It's out of control!

252
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:15,120
Oh, it's a bougie jacuzzi, too!

253
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:16,560
Wanna hop in with me?

254
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,040
I'm totally kidding, dude!

255
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,900
Just sit back and chillax!

256
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:26,800
Nope! Can't do it!

257
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:29,380
Relaxation is not possible!

258
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:33,020
I agree that letting all that money go to waste

259
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,440
is not the ideal situation,

260
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,740
but still...

261
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:38,240
Chitagawa, please!

262
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,520
We have to go!

263
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:40,940
This is not good!

264
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,340
I'll just watch TV.

265
